WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Well, how important was football to LSU?

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.120
When I was there, that was something we’d go to.

3
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.380
We got free tickets.

4
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.360
The students got free tickets to go and . . . I don’t know,

5
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:21.620
I’d guess we’d see three or four thousand people to a game. [laughing] That was a . . . that was a pretty big . . . a big deal.

6
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:29.320
Football players themselves were . . . They were a little rough and tough and . . . I mean,

7
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:38.740
they were not heroes and the rest of the students couldn’t really decide, you know, whether they were one of them or not.

8
00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:49.800
We had this huge man named Jack Torrance that they . . . biggest football player of all times, they’d got some place.

9
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:57.260
I don’t know where they got him, but . . . And they were very disappointed in him because he was so much bigger than everybody,

10
00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.640
he was afraid to . . . he might hurt ’em.

11
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:06.140
And so, he kept up his part of the line alright, but that was about it.

12
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:10.180
Football wasn’t like it is today, those boys.
